<title>NETHERLANDS: WOLTERS/WLSNC.AS/ SEES EPS GROWTH AT LEAST 15 PCT.</title>
<headline>WOLTERS/WLSNC.AS/ SEES EPS GROWTH AT LEAST 15 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch publisher Wolters Kluwer NV said on Friday it would continue to target annual growth of earnings per share of at least 15 percent in the coming years.</p>
<p>The company earlier reported a 1996 net profit of 479 million guilders, up from 452 million in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;The target of Wolters Kluwer for growth in net earnings per &quot;fully diluted&quot; share for the years 1997-1999 is again at least 15 percent per year on average,&quot; the company said in a statement accompanying its 1996 results.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
